{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LS6g8QYDqD6Dz12HftTrmQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment plan, based on the \"median\" tier definition provided. I need to provide specific expected results with rationales for why those results would occur at this tier level.\n\nLet me go through each planned experiment and generate predictions consistent with the median tier characteristics:\n\nKey median tier characteristics:\n- C2 partially confirmed (binarized Likert fuzzy)\n- Limited generalization\n- Original preference confound unresolved\n- Binarized Likert sign test boundary results (p=0.04-0.10)\n- Only 1-2/3 judges significant in pairwise\n\n\n- Only 1/3 additional benchmarks replicate the gap\n- Casual-original subset hovering around 50-56% across all judges (p>0.20)\n- Logistic regression showing formality×original interaction as significant\n- n=500 replicates the overall effect but the casual-original subset remains non-significant\n- Projected review score in the 3.3-3.8 range\n\nNow I'm working through the specific predictions for each experiment. For the multi-judge formality pairwise test, I'd expect 1-2 judges to show significance, with Claude-3.5-Sonnet potentially significant while Gemini-2.0-Flash isn't, and cross-judge formal win rates landing in the 0.55-0.68 range. Moving into the multi-benchmark formality experiment...\n\nThe additional benchmarks mostly don't replicate the effect, though one shows the gap while another doesn't. When comparing Likert versus pairwise sensitivity across judges, the Likert ATE p-values cluster around 0.1-0.4 while pairwise p-values are tighter at 0.01-0.08. The tone axis experiment already failed as expected for a negative control. In the pairwise rate control, the casual-original subset stays at 50-56% across judges with the original preference confound showing significance. The scaled n=500 replication successfully captures the overall effect (p<0.05) but the casual-original subset still doesn't reach significance, with formal win rates between 0.55-0.63. Finally, the binarized Likert sign test yields p-values ranging from 0.04-0.12.\n\nThe NLI threshold sensitivity shows results vary depending on the threshold but the core findings hold steady. The consistency filter bias analysis reveals some bias present but nothing that undermines the conclusions. Human NLI validation shows moderate agreement. In the logistic regression, the formality×original interaction reaches significance (p=0.01-0.1) while the formality coefficient itself ranges from p=0.05-0.2.\n\nNow I'm constructing the full YAML output with detailed predictions for each experiment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13343,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13343},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5482b48d-7390-423a-8d88-768b14e0bb85","uuid":"4e4a6356-dc00-4b3b-800c-e104b70566dd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LS6g8QYDqD6Dz12HftTrmQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C2 需要 hedge：\"Likert scoring shows reduced sensitivity to style bias\n  compared to pairwise comparison, though the source of this gap —\n  measurement structure vs. statistical power — remains partially ambiguous.\"\n  Binarized Likert 结果放在 discussion 中作为 open question 而非 main claim 的证据。\n  Original preference confound 成为论文最大 limitation — 诚实承认\n  \"observed formality preference may partly reflect original-text preference\n  correlated with formality\" 并展示 logistic regression interaction。\n  C1 保持（method works），C3 保持（preliminary），C4 调整为\n  \"use pairwise for auditing; interpret with caution when original preference\n  aligns with style axis\"。标题可保留 \"Likert Blindspot\" 但需在 abstract 加 qualifier。\n  泛化叙事从 \"across judges and benchmarks\" 降级为\n  \"demonstrated on GPT-4o with partial replication on [other judge]\"。\n  仍投 EMNLP Main，预期 Findings accept。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 51\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 33\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.647\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.037\n      claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo: 0.510\n      claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi: 0.764\n      claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.52\n      claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.53\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 27\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 21\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.563\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.44\n      gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo: 0.419\n      gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi: 0.697\n      gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.49\n      gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.57\n      n_judges_pairwise_significant: 2  # GPT-4o + Claude Sonnet; Gemini 不显著\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。\n      Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)，\n      刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)，\n      noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅 56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合\n      \"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\" 的 median 约束。\n      Position bias 在 52-57% 范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [Judge, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Casual_wins, Win_rate, \"p (sign)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", 0.006, \"[0.560, 0.797]\"]\n          - [Claude-3.5-Sonnet, 51, 33, 18, \"64.7%\", 0.037, \"[0.510, 0.764]\"]\n          - [Gemini-2.0-Flash, 48, 27, 21, \"56.3%\", 0.440, \"[0.419, 0.697]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot showing formal win rate ± 95% CI for each judge. GPT-4o 和 Claude Sonnet 的 CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 的 CI 跨越 0.50。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了\n      \"across judges\" 的 generalization claim。论文需表述为\n      \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037);\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44), possibly due to\n      lower consistency rate.\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力\n      不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。\n      三个 judge 均参与评估。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 120\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary: 98\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.635\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.076\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo: 0.497\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi: 0.753\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.611\n      alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p: 0.152\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.541\n      alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p: 0.62\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 80\n      mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.78\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary: 62\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 35\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n      mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.48\n      mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      mtbench_claude_sign_test_p: 0.61\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 1  # LLMBar 已确认; AlpacaEval 边界; MT-Bench 不复制\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o 上\n      formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \"边界复制\"。\n      原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)，\n      且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench 不复制因为其评估任务更结构化\n      (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败\n      而是 benchmark 特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映\n      MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality 的挑战。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Win_rate, \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, 55, 38, \"69.1%\", 0.006]\n          - [AlpacaEval, 52, 33, \"63.5%\", 0.076]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 35, 20, \"57.1%\", 0.48]\n      - title: \"Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"69.1%**\", \"64.7%*\", \"56.3%\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"63.5%†\", \"61.1%\", \"54.1%\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"57.1%\", \"54.5%\", \"51.2%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: benchmark (rows) × judge (cols)，cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，星号标注显著性。左上角深色区 (LLMBar × GPT-4o) 到右下角浅色区 (MT-Bench × Gemini) 的渐变。\"\n    analysis: >\n      泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制，\n      MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\"formality bias is most pronounced on\n      instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval) where stylistic\n      variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show\n      attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient\n      when evaluation criteria are well-defined.\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.089\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.41\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.647\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.037\n      claude_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.031\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.78\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.563\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.44\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.076\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate: 0.635\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.076\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: \"marginal\"\n      cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.41\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.076\n      n_combinations_pairwise_sig: 2\n      n_combinations_likert_sig: 0\n      n_combinations_both_nonsig: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median 在 0.01-0.08 范围。\n      核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。\n      这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。\n      Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \"neither\" case，不支持也不反对 C2。\n      AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)，\n      gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。\n      总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \"Likert always misses what pairwise catches\"，\n      只能说 \"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap is large and significant.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise Win%\", \"Pairwise p\", Gap]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 0.102, 0.332, \"69.1%\", 0.006, \"✓ Blindspot\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 0.076, 0.48, \"63.5%\", 0.076, \"~ Marginal\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", 0.041, 0.69, \"57.1%\", 0.48, \"— Neither\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, 0.089, 0.41, \"64.7%\", 0.037, \"✓ Blindspot\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, AlpacaEval, 0.062, 0.54, \"61.1%\", 0.152, \"— Neither\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, 0.031, 0.78, \"56.3%\", 0.44, \"— Neither\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两根 bar（Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value），α=0.05 红色虚线。清晰展示 Likert bar 始终高于 pairwise bar，但仅 2/6 组合 pairwise bar 低于红线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 \"Likert Blindspot\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert p)，\n      但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\"The Likert Blindspot is most\n      clearly observed when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce\n      significant pairwise effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\"\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis — negative control documentation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"negative_control_documented\"\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      both_pass_rate: 0.45\n      failure_mode: \"epistemic_commitment_change\"\n      assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n      hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n      catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n      paper_role: \"C3 negative control\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为\n      推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。\n      Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style axes 都适用，\n      只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Supplementary figure: tone counterfactual 的 NLI 分布，bimodal pattern (高通过 vs 灾难性失败)，标注 assertive→hedging 方向的 6 个 NLI<0.01 cases。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\"content-preserving\n      counterfactual intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic\n      commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging) structurally violates this\n      requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers that NLI\n      correctly identifies as non-entailment.\"\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。\n      量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.618\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.098\n      gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n: 33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins: 24\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.727\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n: 22\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins: 10\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.455\n      claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.588\n      claude_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.18\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.542\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.56\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate: 0.596\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p: 0.21\n      overall_original_preference: \"moderate (55-62% across judges)\"\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.524\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。\n      Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的\n      (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键 confound：formal-original subset 中\n      original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original subset 中\n      original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。\n      这意味着 pairwise_32b 的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference\n      成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate 部分来自 \"judges prefer originals\" 而非\n      纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal win rate 54.5% (p=0.83)\n      是 \"clean\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。\n      跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%，\n      说明 formality 和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, \"Overall orig%\", \"p\", \"Formal-orig orig%\", \"Casual-orig orig%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, \"61.8%\", 0.098, \"72.7%\", \"45.5%\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, \"58.8%\", 0.18, \"68.2%\", \"47.6%\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, \"54.2%\", 0.56, \"60.0%\", \"50.0%\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, \"59.6%\", 0.21, \"70.0%\", \"48.1%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, N, \"Formal Win%\", \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 22, \"54.5%\", 0.832]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, 20, \"52.4%\", 0.88]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, 18, \"50.0%\", 1.0]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 24, \"53.8%\", 0.74]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: formal-original vs casual-original subset 对比。每个 judge 两组 bar，formal-original 显示高 formal win rate（formality+original 同向），casual-original 显示 ≈50%（两者对抗抵消）。视觉化 confound 的系统性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。\n      Casual-original subset 50-56% 不能排除\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的\n      proxy\"这一解释。但也不能确认 — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。\n      这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_cf_generated: 500\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      n_primary: 430\n      n_consistent: 245\n      formal_wins: 148\n      casual_wins: 97\n      formal_win_rate: 0.604\n      sign_test_p: 0.0008\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.543\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.661\n      consistency_rate: 0.57\n      position_bias_A: 0.52\n      casual_orig_n: 110\n      casual_orig_formal_wins: 60\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      casual_orig_p: 0.39\n      power_analysis_mde_at_80pct: 0.07\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.068\n      likert_ate_p_n500: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate 60.4%\n      低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。\n      关键：即使 n=500，casual-original subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5%\n      (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples 对 54.5% 做 sign test\n      power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5% effect。\n      这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)，\n      要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对 C1 构成实质性挑战。\n      Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了，\n      说明 Likert 确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [Metric, \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal win rate\", \"69.1%\", \"60.4%\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p\", 0.006, 0.0008]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"[0.543, 0.661]\"]\n          - [\"Casual-orig formal win%\", \"54.5%\", \"54.5%\"]\n          - [\"Casual-orig p\", 0.832, 0.39]\n          - [\"Likert ATE p\", 0.332, 0.12]\n      - title: \"Table S2: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [Target_effect, \"N required (80% power)\", \"N required in casual-orig subset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"10%\", 200, 200]\n          - [\"5%\", 800, 800]\n          - [\"4.5% (observed casual-orig)\", \"—\", \"~1200\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effect size convergence plot: x=sample size, y=formal win rate。n=100 点在 69.1%，n=500 点在 60.4%，趋势线收敛到 ~58-60%。Shaded CI band 展示 uncertainty 随 n 缩小。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。\n      Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered，\n      而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\"scaled replication confirms\n      the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the casual-original\n      subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains\n      indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly\n      reflect original-text preference.\"\n\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高\n      则计为 formal win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\n    expected_results:\n      n_scored_pairs: 88\n      n_formal_higher: 42\n      n_casual_higher: 28\n      n_tied: 18\n      n_non_tied: 70\n      formal_win_rate_binarized: 0.60\n      sign_test_p: 0.082\n      interpretation: \"boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。\n      p=0.082 处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution —\n      整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是 \"Likert blindspot\" 的一个机制。\n      但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\"），\n      如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。\n      Formal win rate 60% (binarized Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert\n      检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。\n      这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, N_non_tied, \"Formal wins\", \"Win rate\", \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pairwise (position-controlled)\", 55, 38, \"69.1%\", 0.006]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\", 70, 42, \"60.0%\", 0.082]\n          - [\"Likert ATE (paired t-test)\", 88, \"—\", \"ATE=0.10\", 0.332]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三根 bar 并排：Pairwise win rate (69.1%), Binarized Likert win rate (60.0%), Likert direction (formally higher mean, ATE=0.10)。Error bars 展示各自的 uncertainty。中间 bar 的 CI 跨越 50% 边界但中心在右侧。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释：\n      (1) Likert blindspot 是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity —\n      tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert scale 的固有信息损失；\n      (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity；\n      (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。\n      论文需 hedge：\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise\n      from both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly\n      the forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these\n      sources requires future work with continuous scoring scales.\"\n\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_70_n: 92\n      threshold_70_formal_win_rate: 0.655\n      threshold_70_p: 0.015\n      threshold_75_n: 86\n      threshold_75_formal_win_rate: 0.667\n      threshold_75_p: 0.011\n      threshold_80_n: 78\n      threshold_80_formal_win_rate: 0.682\n      threshold_80_p: 0.008\n      threshold_85_n: 66\n      threshold_85_formal_win_rate: 0.697\n      threshold_85_p: 0.005\n      threshold_90_n: 46\n      threshold_90_formal_win_rate: 0.739\n      threshold_90_p: 0.0015\n      threshold_95_n: 30\n      threshold_95_formal_win_rate: 0.762\n      threshold_95_p: 0.006\n      monotonic_trend: true\n      primary_threshold_80_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate 和\n      significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的\n      counterfactuals，style 是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。\n      p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70% 时 p=0.015)，\n      说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。\n      但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30 (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格\n      的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [Threshold, N, \"Formal Win%\", \"p (sign)\", \"Win rate Δ from 80%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"70%\", 92, \"65.5%\", 0.015, \"-2.7%\"]\n          - [\"75%\", 86, \"66.7%\", 0.011, \"-1.5%\"]\n          - [\"80% (primary)\", 78, \"68.2%\", 0.008, \"—\"]\n          - [\"85%\", 66, \"69.7%\", 0.005, \"+1.5%\"]\n          - [\"90%\", 46, \"73.9%\", 0.0015, \"+5.7%\"]\n          - [\"95%\", 30, \"76.2%\", 0.006, \"+8.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=NLI threshold, y1=formal win rate (left axis, ascending line), y2=sample size (right axis, descending line). 两条线交叉展示 quality-quantity tradeoff。α=0.05 shaded region 标注所有点均显著。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds\n      from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without\n      excessive data loss.\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与\n      bias detection sensitivity 正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\n\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n      task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\n    expected_results:\n      n_consistent: 55\n      n_inconsistent: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      consistent_nli_mean: 0.912\n      inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.871\n      nli_diff_p: 0.14\n      consistent_text_length_mean: 287\n      inconsistent_text_length_mean: 312\n      length_diff_p: 0.08\n      consistent_formal_length_mean: 294\n      inconsistent_formal_length_mean: 326\n      task_type_distribution_chi2_p: 0.32\n      consistent_original_formal_pct: 0.60\n      inconsistent_original_formal_pct: 0.58\n      bias_severity: \"mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。\n      Consistent pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的\n      text length (287 vs 312 chars, p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成\n      position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。\n      Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。\n      Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60% vs 58%)，排除了 original preference\n      与 consistency filter 的交互。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis\"\n        columns: [Variable, Consistent, Inconsistent, \"p (diff)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"N\", 55, 43, \"—\"]\n          - [\"NLI mean\", 0.912, 0.871, 0.14]\n          - [\"Text length mean\", 287, 312, 0.08]\n          - [\"Original-formal %\", \"60%\", \"58%\", 0.85]\n          - [\"Task type χ²\", \"—\", \"—\", 0.32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plot: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI 分布和 text length 分布并排。展示 overlap 但 consistent pairs 略向高 NLI / 短 text 偏移。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\"Position-consistency filtering\n      mildly selects for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed\n      effect if judges are more sensitive to formality in shorter responses.\n      However, NLI scores and task-type distributions do not differ significantly\n      between retained and discarded pairs.\"\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。\n      报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      n_nli_pass: 56  # 70% of annotated sample passed NLI\n      n_nli_fail: 24\n      human_agree_nli_pass: 48  # human says content preserved among NLI-pass\n      human_disagree_nli_pass: 8  # human says content NOT preserved but NLI said pass\n      human_agree_nli_fail: 19  # human agrees content changed among NLI-fail\n      human_disagree_nli_fail: 5  # human says content OK but NLI said fail\n      human_nli_agreement_rate: 0.838\n      cohens_kappa: 0.61\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.143  # 8/56\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.208  # 5/24\n      interpretation: \"substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cohen's kappa 0.61 (\"substantial agreement\") 是 NLI-as-proxy 的合理结果。\n      NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative 20.8%)：\n      一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。\n      但 false positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal\n      但不 reverse 它。False negative (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs，\n      这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall 换 precision）。\n      Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent，\n      需要 acknowledge 作为方法论限制。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: preserved\", \"Human: changed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: pass\", 48, 8]\n          - [\"NLI: fail\", 5, 19]\n      - title: \"Table S6: Agreement Metrics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Agreement rate\", \"83.8%\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's κ\", 0.61]\n          - [\"NLI false positive rate\", \"14.3%\"]\n          - [\"NLI false negative rate\", \"20.8%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap (2×2)。NLI pass/fail vs Human preserved/changed。Off-diagonal cells 用红色标注 error cases，annotated with example IDs。\"\n    analysis: >\n      κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述：\n      \"Human validation yields substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based\n      content verification. The NLI gate is slightly over-permissive (14.3%\n      false positive rate), meaning a small fraction of retained pairs may\n      contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate suggests\n      our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated\n      by content-change noise in the retained set.\"\n\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality×original interaction。\n      替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset 作为 clean estimate。\n    expected_results:\n      n_observations: 55  # consistent pairs from pairwise_32b\n      model_formula: \"formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\"\n      intercept: 0.42\n      intercept_p: 0.18\n      formality_coef: 0.38\n      formality_coef_se: 0.24\n      formality_coef_p: 0.11\n      formality_coef_or: 1.46\n      is_original_coef: 0.72\n      is_original_coef_p: 0.023\n      is_original_coef_or: 2.05\n      interaction_coef: -0.89\n      interaction_coef_se: 0.35\n      interaction_coef_p: 0.011\n      interaction_or: 0.41\n      model_aic: 68.3\n      model_pseudo_r2: 0.12\n      casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.54\n      formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.76\n      overall_marginal_formal_prob: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11），\n      interaction p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果：\n      Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后不再显著 (p=0.11)，\n      但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on\n      original preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大\n      (formal-orig formal win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。\n      Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05) — judges 有独立的 original preference，\n      OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。\n      Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect\n      减少到 46% × 41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。\n      这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足，\n      是 formality effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors\"\n        columns: [Predictor, Coefficient, SE, \"p\", \"OR\", \"95% CI (OR)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept\", 0.42, 0.31, 0.18, 1.52, \"[0.83, 2.80]\"]\n          - [\"Formality direction\", 0.38, 0.24, 0.11, 1.46, \"[0.92, 2.33]\"]\n          - [\"Is original\", 0.72, 0.32, 0.023, 2.05, \"[1.10, 3.82]\"]\n          - [\"Formality × Original\", -0.89, 0.35, 0.011, 0.41, \"[0.21, 0.82]\"]\n      - title: \"Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win\"\n        columns: [Condition, \"P(formal win)\", \"95% CI\", N]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Overall\", \"63.0%\", \"[0.50, 0.76]\", 55]\n          - [\"Formal-original (same direction)\", \"76.0%\", \"[0.58, 0.89]\", 33]\n          - [\"Casual-original (opposing)\", \"54.0%\", \"[0.33, 0.74]\", 22]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: x-axis = {formal-original, casual-original}, y-axis = P(formal win)。两点连线陡峭下降 (76% → 54%)，展示 interaction magnitude。50% reference line 标注。Shaded CI bands。\"\n      - \"Odds ratio forest plot: 三个 predictors 的 OR ± 95% CI。Formality 的 CI 跨越 1.0，Is_original 和 Interaction 的 CI 不含 1.0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制\n      original preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference\n      确认 formality bias。但 interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding：\n      \"measurement of style bias via counterfactual comparison is confounded\n      with original-text preference when the style axis correlates with\n      original text characteristics.\"\n      这成为 C4 的核心依据：\"practitioners should control for original preference\n      when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias; casual-original\n      subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\"\n      论文 discussion 需要 3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括：\n      (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题；\n      (2) interaction 的理论解释；\n      (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications；\n      (4) future work — instrumental variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007b\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。\n      Joint gate (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE — negative\"\n      nli_only_pass_rate_at_090: 0.86\n      joint_bs70_nli90: 0.63\n      forward_nli_mean: 0.9476\n      backward_nli_mean: 0.8267\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment\n      0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上\n      结构性不适用（expansion 降低 surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)，\n      剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。\n      Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment\n      失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于\n      expansion/compression）。Direction-aware NLI 作为 methodological contribution\n      展示在 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE — negative\"\n      bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose: 0.46\n      bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise: 0.87\n      asymmetry_explanation: \"concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment); verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\"\n      paper_role: \"C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败：\n      concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)，\n      verbose→concise 87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。\n      这不是 style transfer 失败，是 verification metric 的结构性限制。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \"method applicability conditions\" 讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。\n      P2 优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"likely_deferred\"\n      if_executed_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n      if_executed_formal_win_rate: 0.58\n      if_executed_sign_test_p: 0.24\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化\n      (academic vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同，\n      NLI pass rate ~79% (academic 文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化\n      触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24) 方向一致但不显著 —\n      register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \"不同但不 better/worse\"。\n      论文中最多作为 \"pilot\" 或 appendix mention。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3；\n      如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n      P2 优先级。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"likely_deferred\"\n      if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n      if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate: 0.63\n      if_executed_llama_sign_test_p: 0.05\n      if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama: -0.07  # Llama slightly lower NLI\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter\n      NLI pass rate 稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer\n      可能更激进导致更多 content change。但 formal win rate 和 significance\n      方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific artifact。\n      不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差，\n      这不是确定性复制。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。\n      如果不执行：在 limitations 中 acknowledge \"counterfactual generation\n      was performed with a single model family (Qwen3-32B); future work\n      should verify with alternative rewriters.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13343,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13343},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5482b48d-7390-423a-8d88-768b14e0bb85","uuid":"fee15a1b-8f5f-429f-b0ee-7fa19c5799c3"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":295640,"duration_api_ms":296999,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C2 需要 hedge：\"Likert scoring shows reduced sensitivity to style bias\n  compared to pairwise comparison, though the source of this gap —\n  measurement structure vs. statistical power — remains partially ambiguous.\"\n  Binarized Likert 结果放在 discussion 中作为 open question 而非 main claim 的证据。\n  Original preference confound 成为论文最大 limitation — 诚实承认\n  \"observed formality preference may partly reflect original-text preference\n  correlated with formality\" 并展示 logistic regression interaction。\n  C1 保持（method works），C3 保持（preliminary），C4 调整为\n  \"use pairwise for auditing; interpret with caution when original preference\n  aligns with style axis\"。标题可保留 \"Likert Blindspot\" 但需在 abstract 加 qualifier。\n  泛化叙事从 \"across judges and benchmarks\" 降级为\n  \"demonstrated on GPT-4o with partial replication on [other judge]\"。\n  仍投 EMNLP Main，预期 Findings accept。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 51\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 33\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.647\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.037\n      claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo: 0.510\n      claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi: 0.764\n      claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.52\n      claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.53\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 27\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 21\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.563\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.44\n      gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo: 0.419\n      gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi: 0.697\n      gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.49\n      gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.57\n      n_judges_pairwise_significant: 2  # GPT-4o + Claude Sonnet; Gemini 不显著\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。\n      Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)，\n      刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)，\n      noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅 56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合\n      \"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\" 的 median 约束。\n      Position bias 在 52-57% 范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [Judge, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Casual_wins, Win_rate, \"p (sign)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", 0.006, \"[0.560, 0.797]\"]\n          - [Claude-3.5-Sonnet, 51, 33, 18, \"64.7%\", 0.037, \"[0.510, 0.764]\"]\n          - [Gemini-2.0-Flash, 48, 27, 21, \"56.3%\", 0.440, \"[0.419, 0.697]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot showing formal win rate ± 95% CI for each judge. GPT-4o 和 Claude Sonnet 的 CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 的 CI 跨越 0.50。\"\n    analysis: >\n      2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了\n      \"across judges\" 的 generalization claim。论文需表述为\n      \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037);\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44), possibly due to\n      lower consistency rate.\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力\n      不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。\n      三个 judge 均参与评估。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 120\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary: 98\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.635\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.076\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo: 0.497\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi: 0.753\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.611\n      alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p: 0.152\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.541\n      alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p: 0.62\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 80\n      mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.78\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary: 62\n      mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 35\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n      mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.48\n      mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      mtbench_claude_sign_test_p: 0.61\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 1  # LLMBar 已确认; AlpacaEval 边界; MT-Bench 不复制\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o 上\n      formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \"边界复制\"。\n      原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)，\n      且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench 不复制因为其评估任务更结构化\n      (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败\n      而是 benchmark 特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映\n      MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality 的挑战。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Win_rate, \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, 55, 38, \"69.1%\", 0.006]\n          - [AlpacaEval, 52, 33, \"63.5%\", 0.076]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 35, 20, \"57.1%\", 0.48]\n      - title: \"Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"69.1%**\", \"64.7%*\", \"56.3%\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"63.5%†\", \"61.1%\", \"54.1%\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"57.1%\", \"54.5%\", \"51.2%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: benchmark (rows) × judge (cols)，cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，星号标注显著性。左上角深色区 (LLMBar × GPT-4o) 到右下角浅色区 (MT-Bench × Gemini) 的渐变。\"\n    analysis: >\n      泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制，\n      MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\"formality bias is most pronounced on\n      instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval) where stylistic\n      variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show\n      attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient\n      when evaluation criteria are well-defined.\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.089\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.41\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.647\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.037\n      claude_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.031\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.78\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.563\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.44\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.076\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate: 0.635\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.076\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: \"marginal\"\n      cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.41\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.076\n      n_combinations_pairwise_sig: 2\n      n_combinations_likert_sig: 0\n      n_combinations_both_nonsig: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median 在 0.01-0.08 范围。\n      核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。\n      这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。\n      Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \"neither\" case，不支持也不反对 C2。\n      AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)，\n      gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。\n      总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \"Likert always misses what pairwise catches\"，\n      只能说 \"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap is large and significant.\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise Win%\", \"Pairwise p\", Gap]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 0.102, 0.332, \"69.1%\", 0.006, \"✓ Blindspot\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 0.076, 0.48, \"63.5%\", 0.076, \"~ Marginal\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", 0.041, 0.69, \"57.1%\", 0.48, \"— Neither\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, 0.089, 0.41, \"64.7%\", 0.037, \"✓ Blindspot\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, AlpacaEval, 0.062, 0.54, \"61.1%\", 0.152, \"— Neither\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, 0.031, 0.78, \"56.3%\", 0.44, \"— Neither\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两根 bar（Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value），α=0.05 红色虚线。清晰展示 Likert bar 始终高于 pairwise bar，但仅 2/6 组合 pairwise bar 低于红线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 \"Likert Blindspot\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert p)，\n      但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\"The Likert Blindspot is most\n      clearly observed when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce\n      significant pairwise effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\"\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis — negative control documentation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"negative_control_documented\"\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      both_pass_rate: 0.45\n      failure_mode: \"epistemic_commitment_change\"\n      assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n      hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n      catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n      paper_role: \"C3 negative control\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为\n      推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。\n      Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style axes 都适用，\n      只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Supplementary figure: tone counterfactual 的 NLI 分布，bimodal pattern (高通过 vs 灾难性失败)，标注 assertive→hedging 方向的 6 个 NLI<0.01 cases。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\"content-preserving\n      counterfactual intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic\n      commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging) structurally violates this\n      requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers that NLI\n      correctly identifies as non-entailment.\"\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。\n      量化 original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.618\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.098\n      gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n: 33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins: 24\n      gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.727\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n: 22\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins: 10\n      gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.455\n      claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.588\n      claude_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.18\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.542\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.56\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate: 0.596\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p: 0.21\n      overall_original_preference: \"moderate (55-62% across judges)\"\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.524\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。\n      Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的\n      (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键 confound：formal-original subset 中\n      original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original subset 中\n      original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。\n      这意味着 pairwise_32b 的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference\n      成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate 部分来自 \"judges prefer originals\" 而非\n      纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal win rate 54.5% (p=0.83)\n      是 \"clean\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。\n      跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%，\n      说明 formality 和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, \"Overall orig%\", \"p\", \"Formal-orig orig%\", \"Casual-orig orig%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, \"61.8%\", 0.098, \"72.7%\", \"45.5%\"]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, \"58.8%\", 0.18, \"68.2%\", \"47.6%\"]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, \"54.2%\", 0.56, \"60.0%\", \"50.0%\"]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, \"59.6%\", 0.21, \"70.0%\", \"48.1%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, N, \"Formal Win%\", \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 22, \"54.5%\", 0.832]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, LLMBar, 20, \"52.4%\", 0.88]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, LLMBar, 18, \"50.0%\", 1.0]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 24, \"53.8%\", 0.74]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar: formal-original vs casual-original subset 对比。每个 judge 两组 bar，formal-original 显示高 formal win rate（formality+original 同向），casual-original 显示 ≈50%（两者对抗抵消）。视觉化 confound 的系统性。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。\n      Casual-original subset 50-56% 不能排除\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的\n      proxy\"这一解释。但也不能确认 — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。\n      这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_cf_generated: 500\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      n_primary: 430\n      n_consistent: 245\n      formal_wins: 148\n      casual_wins: 97\n      formal_win_rate: 0.604\n      sign_test_p: 0.0008\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.543\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.661\n      consistency_rate: 0.57\n      position_bias_A: 0.52\n      casual_orig_n: 110\n      casual_orig_formal_wins: 60\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      casual_orig_p: 0.39\n      power_analysis_mde_at_80pct: 0.07\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.068\n      likert_ate_p_n500: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate 60.4%\n      低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。\n      关键：即使 n=500，casual-original subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5%\n      (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples 对 54.5% 做 sign test\n      power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5% effect。\n      这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)，\n      要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对 C1 构成实质性挑战。\n      Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了，\n      说明 Likert 确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [Metric, \"n=100\", \"n=500\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal win rate\", \"69.1%\", \"60.4%\"]\n          - [\"Sign test p\", 0.006, 0.0008]\n          - [\"95% CI\", \"[0.560, 0.797]\", \"[0.543, 0.661]\"]\n          - [\"Casual-orig formal win%\", \"54.5%\", \"54.5%\"]\n          - [\"Casual-orig p\", 0.832, 0.39]\n          - [\"Likert ATE p\", 0.332, 0.12]\n      - title: \"Table S2: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [Target_effect, \"N required (80% power)\", \"N required in casual-orig subset\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"10%\", 200, 200]\n          - [\"5%\", 800, 800]\n          - [\"4.5% (observed casual-orig)\", \"—\", \"~1200\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effect size convergence plot: x=sample size, y=formal win rate。n=100 点在 69.1%，n=500 点在 60.4%，趋势线收敛到 ~58-60%。Shaded CI band 展示 uncertainty 随 n 缩小。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。\n      Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered，\n      而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\"scaled replication confirms\n      the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the casual-original\n      subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains\n      indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly\n      reflect original-text preference.\"\n\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高\n      则计为 formal win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\n    expected_results:\n      n_scored_pairs: 88\n      n_formal_higher: 42\n      n_casual_higher: 28\n      n_tied: 18\n      n_non_tied: 70\n      formal_win_rate_binarized: 0.60\n      sign_test_p: 0.082\n      interpretation: \"boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。\n      p=0.082 处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution —\n      整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是 \"Likert blindspot\" 的一个机制。\n      但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\"），\n      如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。\n      Formal win rate 60% (binarized Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert\n      检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。\n      这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\"\n        columns: [Method, N_non_tied, \"Formal wins\", \"Win rate\", \"p (sign)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pairwise (position-controlled)\", 55, 38, \"69.1%\", 0.006]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\", 70, 42, \"60.0%\", 0.082]\n          - [\"Likert ATE (paired t-test)\", 88, \"—\", \"ATE=0.10\", 0.332]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三根 bar 并排：Pairwise win rate (69.1%), Binarized Likert win rate (60.0%), Likert direction (formally higher mean, ATE=0.10)。Error bars 展示各自的 uncertainty。中间 bar 的 CI 跨越 50% 边界但中心在右侧。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释：\n      (1) Likert blindspot 是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity —\n      tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert scale 的固有信息损失；\n      (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity；\n      (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。\n      论文需 hedge：\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise\n      from both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly\n      the forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these\n      sources requires future work with continuous scoring scales.\"\n\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_70_n: 92\n      threshold_70_formal_win_rate: 0.655\n      threshold_70_p: 0.015\n      threshold_75_n: 86\n      threshold_75_formal_win_rate: 0.667\n      threshold_75_p: 0.011\n      threshold_80_n: 78\n      threshold_80_formal_win_rate: 0.682\n      threshold_80_p: 0.008\n      threshold_85_n: 66\n      threshold_85_formal_win_rate: 0.697\n      threshold_85_p: 0.005\n      threshold_90_n: 46\n      threshold_90_formal_win_rate: 0.739\n      threshold_90_p: 0.0015\n      threshold_95_n: 30\n      threshold_95_formal_win_rate: 0.762\n      threshold_95_p: 0.006\n      monotonic_trend: true\n      primary_threshold_80_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate 和\n      significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的\n      counterfactuals，style 是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。\n      p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70% 时 p=0.015)，\n      说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。\n      但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30 (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格\n      的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [Threshold, N, \"Formal Win%\", \"p (sign)\", \"Win rate Δ from 80%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"70%\", 92, \"65.5%\", 0.015, \"-2.7%\"]\n          - [\"75%\", 86, \"66.7%\", 0.011, \"-1.5%\"]\n          - [\"80% (primary)\", 78, \"68.2%\", 0.008, \"—\"]\n          - [\"85%\", 66, \"69.7%\", 0.005, \"+1.5%\"]\n          - [\"90%\", 46, \"73.9%\", 0.0015, \"+5.7%\"]\n          - [\"95%\", 30, \"76.2%\", 0.006, \"+8.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: x=NLI threshold, y1=formal win rate (left axis, ascending line), y2=sample size (right axis, descending line). 两条线交叉展示 quality-quantity tradeoff。α=0.05 shaded region 标注所有点均显著。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds\n      from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without\n      excessive data loss.\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与\n      bias detection sensitivity 正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\n\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n      task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\n    expected_results:\n      n_consistent: 55\n      n_inconsistent: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      consistent_nli_mean: 0.912\n      inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.871\n      nli_diff_p: 0.14\n      consistent_text_length_mean: 287\n      inconsistent_text_length_mean: 312\n      length_diff_p: 0.08\n      consistent_formal_length_mean: 294\n      inconsistent_formal_length_mean: 326\n      task_type_distribution_chi2_p: 0.32\n      consistent_original_formal_pct: 0.60\n      inconsistent_original_formal_pct: 0.58\n      bias_severity: \"mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。\n      Consistent pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的\n      text length (287 vs 312 chars, p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成\n      position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。\n      Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。\n      Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60% vs 58%)，排除了 original preference\n      与 consistency filter 的交互。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis\"\n        columns: [Variable, Consistent, Inconsistent, \"p (diff)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"N\", 55, 43, \"—\"]\n          - [\"NLI mean\", 0.912, 0.871, 0.14]\n          - [\"Text length mean\", 287, 312, 0.08]\n          - [\"Original-formal %\", \"60%\", \"58%\", 0.85]\n          - [\"Task type χ²\", \"—\", \"—\", 0.32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Violin plot: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI 分布和 text length 分布并排。展示 overlap 但 consistent pairs 略向高 NLI / 短 text 偏移。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\"Position-consistency filtering\n      mildly selects for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed\n      effect if judges are more sensitive to formality in shorter responses.\n      However, NLI scores and task-type distributions do not differ significantly\n      between retained and discarded pairs.\"\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。\n      报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's kappa)。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      n_nli_pass: 56  # 70% of annotated sample passed NLI\n      n_nli_fail: 24\n      human_agree_nli_pass: 48  # human says content preserved among NLI-pass\n      human_disagree_nli_pass: 8  # human says content NOT preserved but NLI said pass\n      human_agree_nli_fail: 19  # human agrees content changed among NLI-fail\n      human_disagree_nli_fail: 5  # human says content OK but NLI said fail\n      human_nli_agreement_rate: 0.838\n      cohens_kappa: 0.61\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.143  # 8/56\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.208  # 5/24\n      interpretation: \"substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cohen's kappa 0.61 (\"substantial agreement\") 是 NLI-as-proxy 的合理结果。\n      NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative 20.8%)：\n      一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。\n      但 false positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal\n      但不 reverse 它。False negative (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs，\n      这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall 换 precision）。\n      Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent，\n      需要 acknowledge 作为方法论限制。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: preserved\", \"Human: changed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: pass\", 48, 8]\n          - [\"NLI: fail\", 5, 19]\n      - title: \"Table S6: Agreement Metrics\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Agreement rate\", \"83.8%\"]\n          - [\"Cohen's κ\", 0.61]\n          - [\"NLI false positive rate\", \"14.3%\"]\n          - [\"NLI false negative rate\", \"20.8%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap (2×2)。NLI pass/fail vs Human preserved/changed。Off-diagonal cells 用红色标注 error cases，annotated with example IDs。\"\n    analysis: >\n      κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述：\n      \"Human validation yields substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based\n      content verification. The NLI gate is slightly over-permissive (14.3%\n      false positive rate), meaning a small fraction of retained pairs may\n      contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate suggests\n      our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated\n      by content-change noise in the retained set.\"\n\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality×original interaction。\n      替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset 作为 clean estimate。\n    expected_results:\n      n_observations: 55  # consistent pairs from pairwise_32b\n      model_formula: \"formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\"\n      intercept: 0.42\n      intercept_p: 0.18\n      formality_coef: 0.38\n      formality_coef_se: 0.24\n      formality_coef_p: 0.11\n      formality_coef_or: 1.46\n      is_original_coef: 0.72\n      is_original_coef_p: 0.023\n      is_original_coef_or: 2.05\n      interaction_coef: -0.89\n      interaction_coef_se: 0.35\n      interaction_coef_p: 0.011\n      interaction_or: 0.41\n      model_aic: 68.3\n      model_pseudo_r2: 0.12\n      casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.54\n      formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.76\n      overall_marginal_formal_prob: 0.63\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11），\n      interaction p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果：\n      Formality main effect 在控制 original preference 后不再显著 (p=0.11)，\n      但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on\n      original preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大\n      (formal-orig formal win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。\n      Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05) — judges 有独立的 original preference，\n      OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。\n      Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect\n      减少到 46% × 41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。\n      这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足，\n      是 formality effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors\"\n        columns: [Predictor, Coefficient, SE, \"p\", \"OR\", \"95% CI (OR)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept\", 0.42, 0.31, 0.18, 1.52, \"[0.83, 2.80]\"]\n          - [\"Formality direction\", 0.38, 0.24, 0.11, 1.46, \"[0.92, 2.33]\"]\n          - [\"Is original\", 0.72, 0.32, 0.023, 2.05, \"[1.10, 3.82]\"]\n          - [\"Formality × Original\", -0.89, 0.35, 0.011, 0.41, \"[0.21, 0.82]\"]\n      - title: \"Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win\"\n        columns: [Condition, \"P(formal win)\", \"95% CI\", N]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Overall\", \"63.0%\", \"[0.50, 0.76]\", 55]\n          - [\"Formal-original (same direction)\", \"76.0%\", \"[0.58, 0.89]\", 33]\n          - [\"Casual-original (opposing)\", \"54.0%\", \"[0.33, 0.74]\", 22]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Interaction plot: x-axis = {formal-original, casual-original}, y-axis = P(formal win)。两点连线陡峭下降 (76% → 54%)，展示 interaction magnitude。50% reference line 标注。Shaded CI bands。\"\n      - \"Odds ratio forest plot: 三个 predictors 的 OR ± 95% CI。Formality 的 CI 跨越 1.0，Is_original 和 Interaction 的 CI 不含 1.0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制\n      original preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference\n      确认 formality bias。但 interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding：\n      \"measurement of style bias via counterfactual comparison is confounded\n      with original-text preference when the style axis correlates with\n      original text characteristics.\"\n      这成为 C4 的核心依据：\"practitioners should control for original preference\n      when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias; casual-original\n      subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\"\n      论文 discussion 需要 3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括：\n      (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题；\n      (2) interaction 的理论解释；\n      (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications；\n      (4) future work — instrumental variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007b\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。\n      Joint gate (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE — negative\"\n      nli_only_pass_rate_at_090: 0.86\n      joint_bs70_nli90: 0.63\n      forward_nli_mean: 0.9476\n      backward_nli_mean: 0.8267\n      stop_reason: \"NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment\n      0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上\n      结构性不适用（expansion 降低 surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)，\n      剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。\n      Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment\n      失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于\n      expansion/compression）。Direction-aware NLI 作为 methodological contribution\n      展示在 appendix。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity method boundary analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE — negative\"\n      bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose: 0.46\n      bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise: 0.87\n      asymmetry_explanation: \"concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment); verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\"\n      paper_role: \"C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败：\n      concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)，\n      verbose→concise 87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。\n      这不是 style transfer 失败，是 verification metric 的结构性限制。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \"method applicability conditions\" 讨论。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。\n      P2 优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"likely_deferred\"\n      if_executed_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n      if_executed_formal_win_rate: 0.58\n      if_executed_sign_test_p: 0.24\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化\n      (academic vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同，\n      NLI pass rate ~79% (academic 文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化\n      触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24) 方向一致但不显著 —\n      register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \"不同但不 better/worse\"。\n      论文中最多作为 \"pilot\" 或 appendix mention。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3；\n      如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n      P2 优先级。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"likely_deferred\"\n      if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n      if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate: 0.63\n      if_executed_llama_sign_test_p: 0.05\n      if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama: -0.07  # Llama slightly lower NLI\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter\n      NLI pass rate 稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer\n      可能更激进导致更多 content change。但 formal win rate 和 significance\n      方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific artifact。\n      不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差，\n      这不是确定性复制。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。\n      如果不执行：在 limitations 中 acknowledge \"counterfactual generation\n      was performed with a single model family (Qwen3-32B); future work\n      should verify with alternative rewriters.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5482b48d-7390-423a-8d88-768b14e0bb85","total_cost_usd":0.46794024999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13343,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":14808,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13343,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14808,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13343},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8301,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008416,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14808,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13343,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.45952424999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"670a288b-099f-424a-b513-645191ef7b6a"}
